1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,740
Hello everyone, and welcome to Two Cups English.

2
00:00:03,840 --> 00:00:06,720
I'm Mia, and Ben is here with me.

3
00:00:06,780 --> 00:00:09,580
This podcast is for people who are learning English.

4
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:11,080
We speak slowly.

5
00:00:11,620 --> 00:00:12,980
We use simple words.

6
00:00:13,560 --> 00:00:16,400
And we repeat the important words many times.

7
00:00:17,320 --> 00:00:21,640
Today, our topic is small steps every morning.

8
00:00:21,720 --> 00:00:25,030
A small step is one small thing you do to start the day.

9
00:00:26,120 --> 00:00:28,700
Ben, how was your morning today?

10
00:00:28,780 --> 00:00:29,440
Hi Mia.

11
00:00:29,960 --> 00:00:30,560
Hi everyone.

12
00:00:31,440 --> 00:00:34,600
My morning today was slow, but it started.

13
00:00:35,540 --> 00:00:38,820
I woke up, and I did not want to get up.

14
00:00:39,660 --> 00:00:40,840
My room was dark.

15
00:00:41,640 --> 00:00:43,600
My list for the day was long.

16
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:46,320
So I did one small thing.

17
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:48,449
I drank a glass of water.

18
00:00:49,660 --> 00:00:51,920
And then the day started.

19
00:00:51,930 --> 00:00:53,620
Not a perfect morning.

20
00:00:53,700 --> 00:00:54,780
Just a morning.

21
00:00:55,840 --> 00:00:57,200
What about you, Mia?

22
00:00:57,260 --> 00:00:58,240
Did you want to get up?

23
00:00:59,520 --> 00:01:01,860
No, Ben, I did not want to get up.

24
00:01:02,560 --> 00:01:03,600
I looked at the ceiling.

25
00:01:04,180 --> 00:01:06,000
My phone was full of messages.

26
00:01:06,660 --> 00:01:11,860
And I thought, "Today is going to be hard." But then I made my bed.

27
00:01:12,460 --> 00:01:13,760
It took two minutes.

28
00:01:14,240 --> 00:01:16,259
And my morning started, like yours.

29
00:01:17,220 --> 00:01:18,740
I think many people feel this.

30
00:01:19,190 --> 00:01:21,540
The morning is the hardest part of the day.

31
00:01:22,440 --> 00:01:24,100
The hardest part of the day.

32
00:01:24,800 --> 00:01:25,380
Yes, Mia.

33
00:01:26,240 --> 00:01:29,260
For me, the problem was always the big plan.

34
00:01:30,240 --> 00:01:36,200
Every morning I said, "Today I will change my life." Exercise.

35
00:01:36,980 --> 00:01:37,330
Reading.

36
00:01:38,260 --> 00:01:38,820
Good food.

37
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:40,880
One hour of study.

38
00:01:41,880 --> 00:01:44,180
Four big things before eight o'clock.

39
00:01:45,360 --> 00:01:48,620
And every morning, I did none of them.

40
00:01:49,600 --> 00:01:50,520
Do you know that feeling?

41
00:01:51,600 --> 00:01:53,700
I know it very well, Ben.

42
00:01:53,740 --> 00:01:57,080
When I look at the whole day, I feel tired before I start.

43
00:01:57,880 --> 00:01:59,000
Work feels big.

44
00:01:59,760 --> 00:02:01,020
Study feels big.

45
00:02:01,800 --> 00:02:03,940
Even a small message feels big.

46
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:06,880
So what changed for you?

47
00:02:06,980 --> 00:02:08,780
How did you stop the big plan?

48
00:02:09,759 --> 00:02:11,300
Something very simple, Mia.

49
00:02:12,400 --> 00:02:15,540
I learned that a morning does not need a big plan.

50
00:02:16,480 --> 00:02:19,020
A morning needs one small step.

51
00:02:19,800 --> 00:02:20,560
Not four.

52
00:02:21,620 --> 00:02:23,140
And that is our topic today.

53
00:02:24,240 --> 00:02:25,420
So here is our plan.

54
00:02:26,380 --> 00:02:29,160
In part one, we talk about our own mornings.

55
00:02:30,040 --> 00:02:32,680
Our small steps, one by one.

56
00:02:33,700 --> 00:02:36,980
In part two, we ask why small steps work.

57
00:02:37,980 --> 00:02:39,920
And I have a true story for that.

58
00:02:41,040 --> 00:02:44,580
In part three, we share simple ideas for tomorrow morning.

59
00:02:45,540 --> 00:02:46,359
Does that sound good?

60
00:02:47,360 --> 00:02:48,360
That sounds good, Ben.

61
00:02:49,040 --> 00:02:53,040
And to everyone listening, please do not worry if you miss something.

62
00:02:53,580 --> 00:02:54,500
You will hear it again.

63
00:02:55,140 --> 00:02:59,380
You can listen while you walk, while you cook, or while you drink your tea.

64
00:03:00,320 --> 00:03:00,900
Okay, Ben.

65
00:03:01,200 --> 00:03:01,700
Part one.

66
00:03:02,300 --> 00:03:04,420
Tell me about your first small step.

67
00:03:05,160 --> 00:03:07,120
What is the very first thing you do?

68
00:03:08,120 --> 00:03:09,120
Okay, part one.

69
00:03:10,080 --> 00:03:13,000
My first small step is a glass of water.

70
00:03:14,020 --> 00:03:14,600
That is all.

71
00:03:15,620 --> 00:03:19,150
Before coffee, before my phone, before anything.

72
00:03:20,380 --> 00:03:22,180
I put the glass next to my bed at night.

73
00:03:23,020 --> 00:03:25,310
So in the morning, the water is right there.

74
00:03:26,440 --> 00:03:27,660
I do not need to think.

75
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:29,740
I do not need to choose.

76
00:03:30,460 --> 00:03:31,300
I just drink.

77
00:03:32,300 --> 00:03:33,660
It takes twenty seconds.

78
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:35,920
What is your first step, Mia?

79
00:03:36,780 --> 00:03:39,360
My first step is smaller than water, Ben.

80
00:03:40,140 --> 00:03:42,860
When I open my eyes, I do not look at my phone.

81
00:03:43,280 --> 00:03:44,320
That is the first thing.

82
00:03:44,960 --> 00:03:47,580
The phone stays on the table.

83
00:03:47,640 --> 00:03:48,380
Then I sit up.

84
00:03:49,100 --> 00:03:51,200
I put my feet on the floor.

85
00:03:51,440 --> 00:03:53,060
I feel the floor.

86
00:03:53,100 --> 00:03:55,940
It is cold, but it is real.

87
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:58,880
I stay there for ten seconds, and I breathe.

88
00:03:59,780 --> 00:04:00,980
That is my first step.

89
00:04:02,640 --> 00:04:03,980
Feet on the floor, Mia.

90
00:04:04,120 --> 00:04:04,650
I love that.

91
00:04:05,420 --> 00:04:06,610
It is so small.

92
00:04:07,120 --> 00:04:12,140
But it tells your body, "The day starts now." Do you feel different after those ten seconds?

93
00:04:13,320 --> 00:04:14,040
A little, Ben.

94
00:04:14,600 --> 00:04:15,300
Only a little.

95
00:04:15,740 --> 00:04:16,400
Not a lot.

96
00:04:16,940 --> 00:04:18,450
But a little is enough to start.

97
00:04:19,760 --> 00:04:22,200
I think we wait for a big feeling in the morning.

98
00:04:22,700 --> 00:04:24,640
We wait to feel ready.

99
00:04:24,680 --> 00:04:26,920
We wait to feel strong.

100
00:04:26,940 --> 00:04:28,860
But the big feeling does not come.

101
00:04:29,700 --> 00:04:32,400
In the morning, we have only small feelings.

102
00:04:32,940 --> 00:04:34,340
A little sleepy.

103
00:04:34,420 --> 00:04:35,920
A little slow.

104
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:36,860
A little worried.

105
00:04:38,280 --> 00:04:39,740
Only small feelings, Mia.

106
00:04:39,980 --> 00:04:40,740
That is true.

107
00:04:41,479 --> 00:04:43,980
So we need small steps, not big ones.

108
00:04:44,740 --> 00:04:47,540
A small step is something we can do when we feel small.

109
00:04:48,340 --> 00:04:48,860
Sitting up.

110
00:04:49,700 --> 00:04:50,400
Drinking water.

111
00:04:51,320 --> 00:04:52,120
Opening the window.

112
00:04:53,260 --> 00:04:54,260
What is your second step?

113
00:04:54,800 --> 00:04:55,380
After the floor?

114
00:04:56,800 --> 00:04:59,720
After the floor, my second step is my bed, Ben.

115
00:05:00,420 --> 00:05:01,820
I make my bed.

116
00:05:01,900 --> 00:05:03,180
I pull the blanket flat.

117
00:05:03,700 --> 00:05:05,800
I put the pillow in the corner.

118
00:05:05,820 --> 00:05:07,940
It takes two minutes, maybe less.

119
00:05:08,580 --> 00:05:09,600
And then I look at it.

120
00:05:10,180 --> 00:05:10,860
It is neat.

121
00:05:11,420 --> 00:05:12,080
It is done.

122
00:05:12,820 --> 00:05:14,880
This is the first finished thing of my day.

123
00:05:15,520 --> 00:05:16,460
Nobody sees it.

124
00:05:16,840 --> 00:05:19,640
Nobody says "good job." But I see it.

125
00:05:21,100 --> 00:05:26,010
"Nobody says good job, but I see it." That is a beautiful sentence, Mia.

126
00:05:26,730 --> 00:05:28,900
And that small feeling stays with you, right?

127
00:05:29,140 --> 00:05:30,220
It comes with you to work?

128
00:05:31,520 --> 00:05:32,080
Yes, Ben.

129
00:05:32,520 --> 00:05:33,300
It comes with me.

130
00:05:34,060 --> 00:05:36,120
I feel like a person who finishes things.

131
00:05:36,980 --> 00:05:38,260
And what is your second step?

132
00:05:38,720 --> 00:05:39,440
After the water?

133
00:05:41,100 --> 00:05:42,800
My second step is the window, Mia.

134
00:05:43,600 --> 00:05:46,440
I open the window, and I look outside for one minute.

135
00:05:47,120 --> 00:05:47,980
I look at the sky.

136
00:05:48,520 --> 00:05:49,480
I look at the trees.

137
00:05:50,300 --> 00:05:51,400
Sometimes it is raining.

138
00:05:52,200 --> 00:05:53,660
Sometimes a bird is on the roof.

139
00:05:54,540 --> 00:05:55,800
I do not do anything.

140
00:05:56,280 --> 00:05:56,840
I just look.

141
00:05:57,720 --> 00:05:59,760
This one minute changes my morning.

142
00:06:00,680 --> 00:06:02,520
My mind stops thinking about work.

143
00:06:03,240 --> 00:06:04,380
It thinks about the sky.

144
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:08,080
A mind that thinks about the sky, Ben.

145
00:06:08,690 --> 00:06:10,100
That is a calm mind.

146
00:06:11,080 --> 00:06:11,840
And then?

147
00:06:11,900 --> 00:06:13,560
Do you close the window and start the day?

148
00:06:15,020 --> 00:06:17,160
Yes, Mia, but I have one more step.

149
00:06:17,680 --> 00:06:18,420
A third step.

150
00:06:19,209 --> 00:06:19,820
My notebook.

151
00:06:20,770 --> 00:06:22,900
I keep a small notebook on the kitchen table.

152
00:06:23,880 --> 00:06:26,160
Every morning, I write one line.

153
00:06:26,220 --> 00:06:27,660
Only one.

154
00:06:27,700 --> 00:06:28,920
Today's one thing.

155
00:06:29,880 --> 00:06:37,840
For example, "Call the doctor." Or, "Study English for ten minutes." One line, not a list.

156
00:06:38,560 --> 00:06:39,970
A list makes me feel tired.

157
00:06:40,960 --> 00:06:43,440
One line makes me feel clear.

158
00:06:44,260 --> 00:06:45,840
One line, not a list.

159
00:06:46,260 --> 00:06:48,020
Ben, I want to try that.

160
00:06:48,080 --> 00:06:49,860
Because my problem is the list.

161
00:06:50,470 --> 00:06:51,960
My list has ten things.

162
00:06:52,500 --> 00:06:55,500
I finish three, and I feel like I failed.

163
00:06:55,520 --> 00:06:59,300
But if my list has one thing, and I finish it, I win.

164
00:07:00,240 --> 00:07:01,140
You win, Mia.

165
00:07:01,220 --> 00:07:02,360
That is exactly it.

166
00:07:03,040 --> 00:07:04,500
So what is your third step?

167
00:07:04,580 --> 00:07:05,700
After the bed?

168
00:07:05,800 --> 00:07:07,840
My third step is tea, Ben.

169
00:07:08,520 --> 00:07:10,360
I put water in the kettle, and I wait.

170
00:07:10,980 --> 00:07:12,600
This waiting is important.

171
00:07:13,180 --> 00:07:15,000
I do not look at my phone while I wait.

172
00:07:15,600 --> 00:07:17,900
I stand in the kitchen and listen to the water.

173
00:07:18,640 --> 00:07:21,320
It is a small sound, and it grows.

174
00:07:22,140 --> 00:07:24,800
When the tea is ready, I hold the cup with two hands.

175
00:07:25,300 --> 00:07:26,020
It is warm.

176
00:07:26,780 --> 00:07:28,400
I drink slowly.

177
00:07:28,460 --> 00:07:29,560
Five minutes.

178
00:07:30,240 --> 00:07:31,440
Nobody talks to me.

179
00:07:32,400 --> 00:07:34,460
And then I feel ready for people.

180
00:07:35,290 --> 00:07:38,560
"Then I feel ready for people." I understand that, Mia.

181
00:07:39,100 --> 00:07:41,040
Five quiet minutes before the world.

182
00:07:41,920 --> 00:07:45,660
So your morning is feet, bed, tea.

183
00:07:45,720 --> 00:07:46,820
Three small steps.

184
00:07:47,580 --> 00:07:51,120
And mine is water, window, one line.

185
00:07:51,740 --> 00:07:52,340
Also three.

186
00:07:53,220 --> 00:07:54,660
How long do your three steps take?

187
00:07:54,820 --> 00:07:55,280
All together?

188
00:07:55,940 --> 00:07:57,140
Maybe ten minutes, Ben.

189
00:07:57,720 --> 00:07:59,620
Feet on the floor, ten seconds.

190
00:08:00,060 --> 00:08:01,380
Bed, two minutes.

191
00:08:01,800 --> 00:08:03,240
Tea, five minutes.

192
00:08:03,760 --> 00:08:05,300
Ten minutes for the whole morning.

193
00:08:05,780 --> 00:08:07,540
And then I feel like the day has started.

194
00:08:08,700 --> 00:08:10,100
What about your worst morning?

195
00:08:10,620 --> 00:08:12,880
Do you have small steps on a bad day too?

196
00:08:13,700 --> 00:08:15,560
My worst morning, Mia.

197
00:08:15,900 --> 00:08:17,300
Let me tell you.

198
00:08:17,380 --> 00:08:19,560
Last winter, I had a big project at work.

199
00:08:20,340 --> 00:08:22,140
Every morning, I woke up with fear.

200
00:08:22,900 --> 00:08:25,340
I lay in bed and thought about the whole project.

201
00:08:25,920 --> 00:08:26,540
Every part.

202
00:08:27,140 --> 00:08:27,960
Every problem.

203
00:08:28,740 --> 00:08:29,720
My heart went fast.

204
00:08:30,360 --> 00:08:31,140
I did not get up.

205
00:08:31,760 --> 00:08:34,000
I stayed in bed for one hour, thinking.

206
00:08:34,660 --> 00:08:37,380
And after that hour, I felt worse, not better.

207
00:08:38,060 --> 00:08:39,500
Worse, not better.

208
00:08:40,180 --> 00:08:41,660
Ben, I know that hour.

209
00:08:42,280 --> 00:08:44,510
Thinking about the whole thing does not help.

210
00:08:44,920 --> 00:08:46,860
It makes the thing bigger.

211
00:08:46,900 --> 00:08:47,600
What did you do?

212
00:08:48,720 --> 00:08:51,460
One morning, I gave up on the big plan, Mia.

213
00:08:51,520 --> 00:08:52,560
I said, "Okay.

214
00:08:52,680 --> 00:08:53,820
I cannot do the project.

215
00:08:54,310 --> 00:08:57,220
But I can open my laptop." So I got up.

216
00:08:57,720 --> 00:08:58,620
I drank my water.

217
00:08:59,060 --> 00:08:59,960
I opened the window.

218
00:09:00,440 --> 00:09:01,500
I opened my laptop.

219
00:09:02,160 --> 00:09:03,260
That was my only goal.

220
00:09:03,800 --> 00:09:04,900
Open the laptop.

221
00:09:05,720 --> 00:09:10,220
And then I was sitting there, and the laptop was open, so I wrote one sentence.

222
00:09:10,940 --> 00:09:11,460
Then another.

223
00:09:12,380 --> 00:09:14,380
After one hour, I had one page.

224
00:09:15,320 --> 00:09:16,540
One page, Ben.

225
00:09:16,980 --> 00:09:18,340
Not a good page, maybe.

226
00:09:18,680 --> 00:09:19,660
But a page.

227
00:09:20,300 --> 00:09:22,440
And the project was a little smaller after that?

228
00:09:23,220 --> 00:09:24,220
A little smaller, Mia.

229
00:09:24,480 --> 00:09:25,460
Yes.

230
00:09:25,540 --> 00:09:27,109
Every morning, a little smaller.

231
00:09:27,940 --> 00:09:30,980
After ten mornings, it was small enough to hold.

232
00:09:31,080 --> 00:09:32,870
After twenty mornings, it was finished.

233
00:09:33,660 --> 00:09:36,820
And I did not feel brave on any of those mornings.

234
00:09:36,980 --> 00:09:40,080
I just did one small step each morning.

235
00:09:40,090 --> 00:09:41,600
"Brave is not needed.

236
00:09:42,080 --> 00:09:45,840
Small is needed." Ben, I want to put that on my wall.

237
00:09:46,980 --> 00:09:48,440
Okay, so that was part one.

238
00:09:48,940 --> 00:09:49,640
Our mornings.

239
00:09:50,040 --> 00:09:56,540
Feet on the floor, water, a bed, a window, tea, one line in a notebook.

240
00:09:57,080 --> 00:09:58,460
Six small steps.

241
00:09:59,120 --> 00:10:00,100
Now, part two.

242
00:10:00,820 --> 00:10:02,260
Why do small steps work?

243
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:04,660
Ben, you said you have a true story.

244
00:10:05,400 --> 00:10:06,060
I do, Mia.

245
00:10:07,340 --> 00:10:08,180
Okay, part two.

246
00:10:08,760 --> 00:10:10,000
This is a true story.

247
00:10:10,900 --> 00:10:15,020
In 2014, a man named William McRaven gave a speech.

248
00:10:15,640 --> 00:10:17,830
He was an admiral in the United States Navy.

249
00:10:18,640 --> 00:10:20,980
He spoke to students at the University of Texas.

250
00:10:21,580 --> 00:10:24,180
It was their last day at university.

251
00:10:24,220 --> 00:10:26,390
Many people thought he would talk about big things.

252
00:10:26,980 --> 00:10:27,280
War.

253
00:10:27,760 --> 00:10:28,270
Leadership.

254
00:10:28,620 --> 00:10:29,110
The future.

255
00:10:29,900 --> 00:10:31,880
But he started with something very small.

256
00:10:32,580 --> 00:10:34,360
Something very small?

257
00:10:34,400 --> 00:10:35,220
What did he say, Ben?

258
00:10:35,880 --> 00:10:41,700
He said, "If you want to change the world, start by making your bed." That was his first idea, Mia.

259
00:10:42,120 --> 00:10:43,360
To thousands of students.

260
00:10:44,080 --> 00:10:44,860
Make your bed.

261
00:10:45,520 --> 00:10:46,380
Make your bed.

262
00:10:46,920 --> 00:10:50,739
Ben, that is such a small thing to say to thousands of students.

263
00:10:50,780 --> 00:10:52,180
Why did he say that?

264
00:10:52,220 --> 00:10:53,700
He explained why, Mia.

265
00:10:53,780 --> 00:10:56,930
In the Navy, every morning, the instructors checked the beds.

266
00:10:57,430 --> 00:10:59,059
The blanket had to be flat.

267
00:10:59,100 --> 00:11:01,380
The pillow had to be in the right place.

268
00:11:01,440 --> 00:11:02,920
It was a simple task.

269
00:11:03,020 --> 00:11:04,900
Some people thought it was silly.

270
00:11:04,920 --> 00:11:10,120
But McRaven said, when you make your bed, you finish the first task of the day.

271
00:11:10,180 --> 00:11:12,340
It gives a small feeling of pride.

272
00:11:12,360 --> 00:11:14,630
And that small feeling helps with the next task.

273
00:11:15,030 --> 00:11:15,600
And the next.

274
00:11:16,120 --> 00:11:16,760
And the next.

275
00:11:17,540 --> 00:11:19,840
One small task becomes many tasks.

276
00:11:20,260 --> 00:11:21,340
I love that idea, Ben.

277
00:11:21,900 --> 00:11:23,300
And I think he said one more thing.

278
00:11:23,980 --> 00:11:26,940
If we have a bad day, we come home to a bed that is made.

279
00:11:27,480 --> 00:11:28,580
A bed that we made.

280
00:11:29,180 --> 00:11:32,980
And that small thing says, "Tomorrow will be better." Is that right?

281
00:11:33,640 --> 00:11:34,600
That is right, Mia.

282
00:11:35,150 --> 00:11:36,800
That speech became a small book.

283
00:11:37,500 --> 00:11:38,780
Millions of people read it.

284
00:11:39,600 --> 00:11:42,340
Why do you think so many people read a book about making a bed?

285
00:11:43,040 --> 00:11:44,920
Because it is not a big idea, Ben.

286
00:11:45,380 --> 00:11:46,540
It is a small idea.

287
00:11:47,140 --> 00:11:48,940
Everyone can make a bed.

288
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:51,560
Nobody can change the world before breakfast.

289
00:11:51,600 --> 00:11:53,600
But everyone can make a bed.

290
00:11:53,760 --> 00:11:55,280
Small steps are for everyone.

291
00:11:55,720 --> 00:11:56,800
For the tired person.

292
00:11:57,160 --> 00:11:58,140
For the busy person.

293
00:11:58,660 --> 00:12:00,540
For the person who feels sad in the morning.

294
00:12:01,180 --> 00:12:03,760
"Small steps are for everyone." Yes, Mia.

295
00:12:04,420 --> 00:12:06,960
Nobody needs energy for a small step.

296
00:12:07,020 --> 00:12:08,620
Nobody needs a plan.

297
00:12:08,680 --> 00:12:11,780
We need two minutes and one small action.

298
00:12:11,820 --> 00:12:14,000
And there is one more reason small steps work.

299
00:12:14,690 --> 00:12:17,500
The first step decides the shape of the morning.

300
00:12:17,529 --> 00:12:19,020
The shape of the morning?

301
00:12:19,060 --> 00:12:19,800
What do you mean, Ben?

302
00:12:20,520 --> 00:12:23,800
McRaven said the first task matters because it is the first, Mia.

303
00:12:24,280 --> 00:12:25,480
Not because it is important.

304
00:12:26,140 --> 00:12:27,560
Making a bed is not important.

305
00:12:28,100 --> 00:12:30,520
Nobody's life changes because of a flat blanket.

306
00:12:31,100 --> 00:12:34,820
But if the first task is finished, the second task is easier to start.

307
00:12:35,680 --> 00:12:40,140
If the first task is a phone and thirty minutes of scrolling, the second task is harder.

308
00:12:40,929 --> 00:12:42,560
The first step sets the direction.

309
00:12:43,340 --> 00:12:45,580
The first step sets the direction, Ben.

310
00:12:46,280 --> 00:12:55,560
So the question is not, "How do I have a great day?" The question is, "What is my first step?" And the answer should be very small.

311
00:12:56,120 --> 00:12:57,190
Smaller than we think.

312
00:12:57,880 --> 00:12:58,840
Not exercise.

313
00:12:59,259 --> 00:13:00,700
Not one hour of study.

314
00:13:01,640 --> 00:13:02,540
Feet on the floor.

315
00:13:03,400 --> 00:13:03,780
Water.

316
00:13:04,660 --> 00:13:05,130
Window.

317
00:13:06,220 --> 00:13:06,500
Bed.

318
00:13:07,620 --> 00:13:08,270
Just one, Mia.

319
00:13:08,650 --> 00:13:13,320
And the rest of the morning follows that first step, like water follows the first drop.

320
00:13:14,480 --> 00:13:15,329
Can I ask you something?

321
00:13:15,969 --> 00:13:18,630
What do you do when the small step does not work?

322
00:13:19,220 --> 00:13:21,700
When you make your bed, and you still feel bad?

323
00:13:23,080 --> 00:13:24,160
That happens, Ben.

324
00:13:24,820 --> 00:13:27,760
Some mornings, I do my steps, and I still feel bad.

325
00:13:28,300 --> 00:13:32,350
My bed is made, my tea is warm, and my heart is still heavy.

326
00:13:33,210 --> 00:13:36,200
And on those mornings, I try to remember one thing.

327
00:13:36,930 --> 00:13:39,160
The step is not for the feeling.

328
00:13:39,200 --> 00:13:41,580
The step is for the day.

329
00:13:41,590 --> 00:13:47,400
"The step is for the day, not for the feeling." Mia, that is a beautiful answer.

330
00:13:47,520 --> 00:13:50,170
So even if you feel bad, the day has started?

331
00:13:51,100 --> 00:13:51,740
Yes, Ben.

332
00:13:52,500 --> 00:13:54,730
Even if I feel bad, my bed is made.

333
00:13:55,240 --> 00:13:56,740
My body has water.

334
00:13:56,780 --> 00:13:58,780
My day has started.

335
00:13:58,790 --> 00:14:01,700
The good feeling comes later, or it does not come.

336
00:14:02,320 --> 00:14:03,680
But the day starts anyway.

337
00:14:04,260 --> 00:14:05,160
That is enough.

338
00:14:06,200 --> 00:14:07,100
That is enough.

339
00:14:07,760 --> 00:14:10,700
I think many people stop because they wait for the feeling, Mia.

340
00:14:11,370 --> 00:14:20,220
They do the small step one time, they do not feel great, and they say, "It does not work." But the small step is not magic.

341
00:14:20,280 --> 00:14:21,620
It is a start.

342
00:14:21,680 --> 00:14:23,280
The morning does not need to be good.

343
00:14:23,960 --> 00:14:25,840
It needs to begin.

344
00:14:25,870 --> 00:14:29,580
"It needs to begin." Ben, I want to stay with that word.

345
00:14:30,130 --> 00:14:30,600
Start.

346
00:14:31,290 --> 00:14:33,319
We think a start must be big.

347
00:14:33,400 --> 00:14:34,480
A new year.

348
00:14:34,490 --> 00:14:35,520
A new job.

349
00:14:35,580 --> 00:14:36,150
A Monday.

350
00:14:36,980 --> 00:14:39,190
But a start is just the first small step.

351
00:14:39,880 --> 00:14:40,980
I can start at six.

352
00:14:41,360 --> 00:14:42,280
I can start at ten.

353
00:14:42,920 --> 00:14:44,540
I can start again after lunch.

354
00:14:45,360 --> 00:14:45,880
Do you agree?

355
00:14:46,400 --> 00:14:47,680
Can a morning start late?

356
00:14:49,080 --> 00:14:49,800
It can, Mia.

357
00:14:50,460 --> 00:14:51,980
Last week, I woke up late.

358
00:14:52,560 --> 00:14:53,560
No time for water.

359
00:14:54,060 --> 00:14:54,620
No window.

360
00:14:55,240 --> 00:14:56,220
I ran out of the door.

361
00:14:57,100 --> 00:14:59,920
In the past, a morning like that broke my whole day.

362
00:15:00,720 --> 00:15:04,140
But at ten o'clock, at my desk, I drank a glass of water.

363
00:15:04,880 --> 00:15:06,100
That was my small step.

364
00:15:06,700 --> 00:15:07,760
Late, but real.

365
00:15:08,360 --> 00:15:09,420
The morning was gone.

366
00:15:10,010 --> 00:15:11,220
The day was not.

367
00:15:12,320 --> 00:15:16,800
"The morning was gone, but the day was not." That is important, Ben.

368
00:15:17,480 --> 00:15:19,240
Small steps do not have a deadline.

369
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:22,940
If the first step is late, it is still the first step.

370
00:15:23,860 --> 00:15:25,340
Okay, so that was part two.

371
00:15:25,900 --> 00:15:27,600
Why small steps work.

372
00:15:28,300 --> 00:15:29,980
We talked about McRaven and the bed.

373
00:15:30,620 --> 00:15:32,650
We said the first step sets the direction.

374
00:15:33,400 --> 00:15:34,880
Now, part three.

375
00:15:34,960 --> 00:15:37,260
Simple ideas for tomorrow morning.

376
00:15:37,280 --> 00:15:38,290
Ben, you go first.

377
00:15:39,240 --> 00:15:40,740
Okay, part three.

378
00:15:40,780 --> 00:15:42,900
My first idea is about the evening, Mia.

379
00:15:43,570 --> 00:15:46,160
A good morning starts the night before.

380
00:15:46,200 --> 00:15:48,210
Before bed, I fill my glass of water.

381
00:15:48,920 --> 00:15:50,840
I put my clothes for tomorrow on the chair.

382
00:15:51,580 --> 00:15:53,440
I open my notebook to a clean page.

383
00:15:54,260 --> 00:15:56,839
I put my phone on the table, not next to my pillow.

384
00:15:57,580 --> 00:15:58,520
Four small things.

385
00:15:59,000 --> 00:15:59,660
Five minutes.

386
00:16:00,540 --> 00:16:04,200
And in the morning, my first steps are easy, because I prepared them.

387
00:16:05,820 --> 00:16:08,339
The phone on the table, not next to the pillow.

388
00:16:08,990 --> 00:16:11,440
Ben, that one is hard for me.

389
00:16:11,480 --> 00:16:13,020
But I do the same with my cup.

390
00:16:13,440 --> 00:16:14,740
I wash it at night.

391
00:16:14,800 --> 00:16:17,529
In the morning, it is there, clean, waiting.

392
00:16:18,720 --> 00:16:20,480
My first idea is about the key.

393
00:16:21,200 --> 00:16:24,740
My whole morning can break because of a lost key.

394
00:16:24,800 --> 00:16:27,640
So now my key lives in one place.

395
00:16:27,700 --> 00:16:29,500
A small bowl next to the door.

396
00:16:30,360 --> 00:16:32,669
Every evening, the key goes in the bowl.

397
00:16:34,040 --> 00:16:36,820
The answer to a lost key is a bowl.

398
00:16:36,960 --> 00:16:38,320
I love how simple that is, Mia.

399
00:16:39,140 --> 00:16:41,520
We look for big answers to small problems.

400
00:16:42,100 --> 00:16:43,520
But the answer is a bowl.

401
00:16:44,620 --> 00:16:46,660
My second idea is the one line.

402
00:16:47,380 --> 00:16:49,980
Tomorrow morning, write one line in a notebook.

403
00:16:50,760 --> 00:16:51,840
Today's one thing.

404
00:16:52,600 --> 00:16:53,160
Not a list.

405
00:16:53,860 --> 00:16:54,680
One line.

406
00:16:55,460 --> 00:16:59,120
When you finish that one thing, your day is a good day.

407
00:16:59,160 --> 00:17:00,420
Everything else is extra.

408
00:17:01,160 --> 00:17:02,780
Everything else is extra, Ben.

409
00:17:03,280 --> 00:17:03,880
I like that.

410
00:17:04,960 --> 00:17:07,160
My second idea is for the afternoon.

411
00:17:07,800 --> 00:17:10,180
Because small steps are not only for the morning.

412
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:13,280
At two o'clock, my eyes are heavy.

413
00:17:13,940 --> 00:17:17,260
I want to open my phone and look at nothing for thirty minutes.

414
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:19,160
So I stand up.

415
00:17:19,920 --> 00:17:21,120
I walk to the window.

416
00:17:21,840 --> 00:17:23,580
I look outside for one minute.

417
00:17:24,140 --> 00:17:27,320
Then I come back, and I can work again for one hour.

418
00:17:28,120 --> 00:17:29,720
One minute at the window, Mia.

419
00:17:30,200 --> 00:17:31,260
That works for me too.

420
00:17:32,100 --> 00:17:34,800
And in the afternoon, my step is water again.

421
00:17:35,840 --> 00:17:37,600
I know, I talk about water a lot.

422
00:17:38,320 --> 00:17:40,840
But when I feel slow, I am often just thirsty.

423
00:17:41,700 --> 00:17:43,640
Small problems have small answers.

424
00:17:44,420 --> 00:17:46,540
We do not need a new life.

425
00:17:46,580 --> 00:17:49,240
We need a glass of water and one minute at the window.

426
00:17:50,129 --> 00:17:52,540
Small problems have small answers.

427
00:17:53,300 --> 00:17:54,560
Do you have a third idea, Ben?

428
00:17:55,100 --> 00:17:57,240
Something for our listeners who are learning English?

429
00:17:58,120 --> 00:17:59,040
Yes, Mia.

430
00:17:59,080 --> 00:18:00,940
My third idea is ten minutes.

431
00:18:01,820 --> 00:18:03,820
Learning a language is a very big thing.

432
00:18:04,380 --> 00:18:05,240
It takes years.

433
00:18:06,080 --> 00:18:08,140
Nobody can learn English in one morning.

434
00:18:09,020 --> 00:18:10,740
And that is why many people stop.

435
00:18:11,470 --> 00:18:13,879
They look at the whole mountain, and they feel small.

436
00:18:14,820 --> 00:18:17,100
But English is also made of small steps.

437
00:18:18,020 --> 00:18:18,540
One word.

438
00:18:19,160 --> 00:18:19,940
One sentence.

439
00:18:20,720 --> 00:18:22,900
Ten minutes in the morning with a cup of coffee.

440
00:18:23,760 --> 00:18:25,539
That is how I learned Spanish, actually.

441
00:18:26,240 --> 00:18:27,560
Ten minutes with coffee?

442
00:18:28,220 --> 00:18:29,030
Not a class, Ben?

443
00:18:29,960 --> 00:18:30,840
Not a class, Mia.

444
00:18:31,160 --> 00:18:32,320
Ten minutes with my coffee.

445
00:18:32,900 --> 00:18:34,340
I listened to one short thing.

446
00:18:35,060 --> 00:18:38,020
I said the sentences out loud, quietly, in my kitchen.

447
00:18:38,880 --> 00:18:40,700
My neighbor probably thought I was strange.

448
00:18:41,680 --> 00:18:43,740
But after one year, I could talk to people.

449
00:18:44,180 --> 00:18:44,899
Not perfectly.

450
00:18:45,200 --> 00:18:45,880
But I could talk.

451
00:18:46,680 --> 00:18:48,960
And it started with ten minutes and a cup of coffee.

452
00:18:49,660 --> 00:18:51,380
A small step, every morning.

453
00:18:52,380 --> 00:18:55,179
A small step, every morning.

454
00:18:55,300 --> 00:18:58,980
So for everyone listening now, this podcast can be your small step.

455
00:18:59,780 --> 00:19:01,140
Ten minutes, or five.

456
00:19:01,860 --> 00:19:02,640
Listen a little.

457
00:19:03,240 --> 00:19:04,820
Say one sentence out loud.

458
00:19:05,400 --> 00:19:07,240
Then close the video and go to your day.

459
00:19:07,900 --> 00:19:09,300
Tomorrow, listen again.

460
00:19:10,150 --> 00:19:12,060
We are not asking for one hour.

461
00:19:12,700 --> 00:19:14,529
We are asking for a small step.

462
00:19:15,520 --> 00:19:16,480
A small step, Mia.

463
00:19:17,490 --> 00:19:18,780
And I have one last idea.

464
00:19:19,600 --> 00:19:22,840
It is for the people who feel bad about their mornings.

465
00:19:22,920 --> 00:19:24,160
Because I was that person.

466
00:19:24,960 --> 00:19:26,620
I thought I was lazy.

467
00:19:26,780 --> 00:19:30,040
I thought other people had energy, and I did not.

468
00:19:30,110 --> 00:19:34,940
I watched videos of people who wake up at five and run and cook and read.

469
00:19:34,960 --> 00:19:36,920
And I felt worse.

470
00:19:36,980 --> 00:19:38,430
And now, Ben?

471
00:19:38,440 --> 00:19:39,220
What do you think now?

472
00:19:40,280 --> 00:19:42,680
Now I think those videos were not about me, Mia.

473
00:19:43,360 --> 00:19:44,400
My morning is different.

474
00:19:45,100 --> 00:19:46,440
My small steps are different.

475
00:19:46,740 --> 00:19:47,480
And that is fine.

476
00:19:48,460 --> 00:19:50,700
The goal is not a perfect morning.

477
00:19:50,760 --> 00:19:52,380
The goal is a morning that starts.

478
00:19:53,280 --> 00:19:55,640
And I think that is our message today.

479
00:19:55,680 --> 00:19:57,820
We do not need a perfect morning.

480
00:19:57,840 --> 00:19:59,200
We need a morning that starts.

481
00:19:59,940 --> 00:20:02,020
And a morning starts with one small step.

482
00:20:03,180 --> 00:20:04,360
A morning that starts.

483
00:20:05,280 --> 00:20:10,380
Ben, let's repeat today's important words, slowly, because our listeners want to remember them.

484
00:20:11,640 --> 00:20:12,040
Small.

485
00:20:12,660 --> 00:20:13,360
Not big.

486
00:20:14,320 --> 00:20:15,400
A small step.

487
00:20:16,380 --> 00:20:17,480
A small feeling.

488
00:20:18,460 --> 00:20:19,540
A small problem.

489
00:20:20,700 --> 00:20:21,120
Step.

490
00:20:21,820 --> 00:20:22,600
One movement.

491
00:20:23,120 --> 00:20:23,860
One action.

492
00:20:24,980 --> 00:20:26,000
Step by step.

493
00:20:27,160 --> 00:20:27,560
Morning.

494
00:20:27,980 --> 00:20:29,100
The start of the day.

495
00:20:29,920 --> 00:20:30,700
Every morning.

496
00:20:31,640 --> 00:20:32,280
This morning.

497
00:20:33,640 --> 00:20:34,500
Start.

498
00:20:34,510 --> 00:20:35,160
To begin.

499
00:20:36,060 --> 00:20:36,960
The day starts.

500
00:20:37,760 --> 00:20:38,690
We start small.

501
00:20:39,940 --> 00:20:40,209
Feel.

502
00:20:40,920 --> 00:20:42,280
To have a feeling inside.

503
00:20:43,200 --> 00:20:44,100
I feel tired.

504
00:20:44,880 --> 00:20:45,580
I feel ready.

505
00:20:46,420 --> 00:20:47,360
I feel a little better.

506
00:20:48,840 --> 00:20:49,160
Small.

507
00:20:50,220 --> 00:20:50,520
Step.

508
00:20:51,640 --> 00:20:52,110
Morning.

509
00:20:53,240 --> 00:20:53,580
Start.

510
00:20:55,020 --> 00:20:55,340
Feel.

511
00:20:56,660 --> 00:20:57,720
Five small words.

512
00:20:58,280 --> 00:20:59,580
And one small idea.

513
00:21:00,500 --> 00:21:02,580
A morning starts with one small step.

514
00:21:03,600 --> 00:21:06,040
Now, Mia, do you have a question for our listeners?

515
00:21:07,220 --> 00:21:07,780
Yes, Ben.

516
00:21:08,360 --> 00:21:10,320
Everyone listening, here is my question.

517
00:21:10,960 --> 00:21:13,060
What is your first small step tomorrow morning?

518
00:21:13,720 --> 00:21:14,920
Not a plan.

519
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:15,640
Not a list.

520
00:21:16,140 --> 00:21:17,100
Just the first step.

521
00:21:17,860 --> 00:21:19,180
Feet on the floor?

522
00:21:19,260 --> 00:21:20,070
A glass of water?

523
00:21:20,820 --> 00:21:21,300
The window?

524
00:21:22,020 --> 00:21:22,400
The bed?

525
00:21:23,180 --> 00:21:25,580
Write it in the comments in one short sentence.

526
00:21:26,100 --> 00:21:32,720
For example, "Tomorrow, I will drink a glass of water." One sentence is a small step in English.

527
00:21:34,060 --> 00:21:37,500
And if this episode helped you, please subscribe to Two Cups English.

528
00:21:38,240 --> 00:21:40,300
We make a new episode every few days.

529
00:21:41,040 --> 00:21:45,940
Slow English, simple words, and one true story each time.

530
00:21:45,950 --> 00:21:48,309
The full text of this episode is in the description.

531
00:21:49,200 --> 00:21:50,820
Reading while listening helps a lot.

532
00:21:51,420 --> 00:21:52,380
It is free.

533
00:21:52,480 --> 00:21:52,590
Take it.

534
00:21:53,540 --> 00:21:55,339
Thank you for spending this time with us.

535
00:21:55,999 --> 00:21:57,419
Maybe you listened while cooking.

536
00:21:58,139 --> 00:21:59,139
Maybe while walking.

537
00:21:59,919 --> 00:22:02,780
Maybe in bed, in the dark, before sleep.

538
00:22:03,820 --> 00:22:06,439
Wherever you are, we are happy you are here.

539
00:22:07,079 --> 00:22:09,539
And remember, nobody needs a big morning.

540
00:22:10,039 --> 00:22:11,400
We need a small step.

541
00:22:12,279 --> 00:22:12,899
This is Ben.

542
00:22:13,559 --> 00:22:14,279
And this is Mia.

543
00:22:14,920 --> 00:22:16,419
This was Two Cups English.

544
00:22:17,039 --> 00:22:18,080
Start small tomorrow.

545
00:22:18,679 --> 00:22:19,820
We will see you next time.

